From 0000000000000000000000000000000000000000 Mon Sep 17 00:00:00 2001
From: Domenico D'Arrigo <d.darrigo@outlook.it>
Date: Sun, 25 Oct 2026 15:13:16 +0100
Subject: [PATCH] ec/lenovo/h8: Notify the CPUs on AC changes only, not from
 _PSR

_PSR of the AC adapter calls PNOT, which notifies every CPU thread with
0x81 (re-evaluate the processor objects) each time the OS reads the
power source. That is not only on a change: Linux evaluates _PSR on
every read of the online property of the AC power supply, and other
OSes and their drivers poll it.

The EC events that report a change, _Q26 and _Q27, already notify AC and
call PNOT. Leave _PSR to report the state and update PWRS, as before. No
processor object of this platform depends on PWRS.

TEST=Built lenovo/w541 with mrc.bin and with the native RAM init. In
acpiexec, _PSR of AC returns HPAC; before, it went on to \PNOT and
\_SB.CNOT (not found there, as the DSDT was loaded without the SSDT).

Co-authored-by: Claude Opus 5.5 <noreply@anthropic.com>
Claude-Session: https://claude.ai/code/session_018n3yuWwDLW63F4vdf7ZFTv
---
 src/ec/lenovo/h8/acpi/ac.asl | 5 ++++-
 1 file changed, 4 insertions(+), 1 deletion(-)

diff --git a/src/ec/lenovo/h8/acpi/ac.asl b/src/ec/lenovo/h8/acpi/ac.asl
index 436fdcfaeb..0bfee95d05 100644
--- a/src/ec/lenovo/h8/acpi/ac.asl
+++ b/src/ec/lenovo/h8/acpi/ac.asl
@@ -13,11 +13,14 @@ Device(AC)
 	Name(_UID, 0x00)
 	Name(_PCL, Package() { \_SB } )
 
+	/*
+	 * Only reports the state: _Q26 and _Q27 notify the CPUs when it
+	 * changes, and the OS reads _PSR whenever it likes (some poll it).
+	 */
 	Method(_PSR, 0, NotSerialized)
 	{
 		Local0 = HPAC
 		\PWRS = Local0
-		\PNOT()
 		return (Local0)
 	}
 
